Below is a **single‑statement script** that will drop **every user‑defined table** (and the system‑tables that belong to the `[hr_records]` schema if any exist) from the schema `[hr_records]`.  
> ⚠️ **Use with caution** – this will permanently delete all data in those tables. Run it only on a test environment or after a full backup.

```sql
/* 1️⃣  Build drop‑table statements for every table in dbo.hr_records */
DECLARE @sql NVARCHAR(MAX) = N'',
        @t NVARCHAR(128);

-- Grab the object_id of the schema so we can reference it in sys.tables
DECLARE @schema_id INT = SCHEMA_ID(N'hr_records');

-- Get every base table (including views if you want to drop them; they are not included here)
DECLARE table_cursor CURSOR FAST_FORWARD FOR
SELECT QUOTENAME(name) AS tname
FROM sys.tables
WHERE schema_id = @schema_id;      -- only tables in hr_records

OPEN table_cursor;
FETCH NEXT FROM table_cursor INTO @t;

WHILE @@FETCH_STATUS = 0
BEGIN
    -- Append a DROP TABLE statement
    SET @sql += 'DROP TABLE [hr_records].' + @t + ';' + CHAR(13);

    FETCH NEXT FROM table_cursor INTO @t;
END

CLOSE table_cursor;
DEALLOCATE table_cursor;

/* 2️⃣  Execute the script */
PRINT 'The following statements will be executed:';   -- optional for debugging
PRINT @sql;

EXEC sp_executesql @sql;
```

### How it works
1. **Cursor over `sys.tables`** – fetches every table in the `[hr_records]` schema.  
2. **Build a string of `DROP TABLE` statements** – one per table.  
3. **Execute** the complete set with `sp_executesql`.

### If you also want to drop views or other schema objects

```sql
-- add this after the tables loop
SELECT QUOTENAME(name) AS objname
FROM sys.views          -- for views
WHERE schema_id = @schema_id;
```

and change the drop line to:

```sql
SET @sql += 'DROP VIEW [hr_records].' + @t + ';' + CHAR(13);
```

The script above will cover *all* tables created inside `[hr_records]`, and because it references the schema directly, it will also catch any “system” tables that happen to belong to that schema (e.g., those created by custom extensions or internal processes).

