## Quick‑Start: A Mini‑Illustrator in JavaScript

Below is a **minimal yet extensible** JavaScript library that gives you the core building blocks of a vector‑graphics editor:

1. **Shapes** – path, ellipse, rectangle, polyline, polygon.  
2. **Attributes** – fill, stroke, opacity, blend mode, dash‑array.  
3. **Transformations** – translate, rotate, scale, skew, matrix.  
4. **Grouping & Stacking** – groups, layers, z‑order.  
5. **File I/O** – export/import to/from SVG (Illustrator’s AI format is binary and proprietary; SVG is an open, widely‑supported vector format that Illustrator reads/writes just fine).  

> **Why SVG?**  
> - Open standard, human‑readable.  
> - Directly editable in Illustrator.  
> - No licensing headaches.  
> - Good for web and cross‑platform interchange.

> **What’s not covered**:  
> - Complex brushes, gradients, patterns, clipping masks, text layout, and effects (drop‑shadow, warp, etc.).  
> - Advanced interoperability (AI, PDF, EPS).  
> - Performance optimizations for thousands of objects.  

The code below uses **TypeScript** (for type safety, readability) and can be transpiled to plain‑JavaScript for browsers or Node.js.

---

### 1. Project Skeleton

```
mini-illustrator/
│
├─ src/
│   ├─ core/
│   │   ├─ primitives.ts        // Path, Rect, Ellipse, etc.
│   │   ├─ group.ts             // Group and Layer logic
│   │   ├─ transform.ts         // Matrix & transform helpers
│   │   ├─ attributes.ts        // Color/Fill/Stroke/Opacity
│   │   └─ document.ts          // Document, Layers, History
│   │
│   ├─ io/
│   │   ├─ svg.ts               // Import / Export SVG
│   │   └─ helpers.ts
│   │
│   ├─ index.ts                 // Public API
│   └─ utils.ts
│
├─ tests/
│   ├─ primitives.test.ts
│   └─ ...
│
├─ package.json
├─ tsconfig.json
└─ README.md
```

---

### 2. Core Types & Utils

```ts
// src/core/types.ts
export type Point = { x: number; y: number };
export type Color = string; // CSS hex, rgb(), hsl(), etc.

export interface BaseObject {
  id: string;
  type: string;
  attrs: Attributes;
  transform: Transform;
}

export interface Attributes {
  fill?: Color;
  stroke?: Color;
  strokeWidth?: number;
  opacity?: number;           // 0–1
  // ...extend as needed
}

export type Transform = {
  matrix: number[]; // 6-element array for SVG (a, b, c, d, e, f)
};

export type Document = {
  layers: Layer[];
  width: number;
  height: number;
};

export interface Layer {
  name: string;
  objects: BaseObject[];
  opacity?: number;
}
```

```ts
// src/core/utils.ts
export const idGen = (() => {
  let counter = 0;
  return () => `obj-${++counter}`;
})();

export function identityMatrix(): Transform {
  return { matrix: [1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0] };
}
```

---

### 3. Transform Helpers

```ts
// src/core/transform.ts
export function multiplyMatrices(a: number[], b: number[]): number[] {
  const [a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6] = a;
  const [b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6] = b;
  return [
    a1 * b1 + a3 * b2,
    a2 * b1 + a4 * b2,
    a1 * b3 + a3 * b4,
    a2 * b3 + a4 * b4,
    a1 * b5 + a3 * b6 + a5,
    a2 * b5 + a4 * b6 + a6,
  ];
}

export function translate(tx: number, ty: number): number[] {
  return [1, 0, 0, 1, tx, ty];
}

export function rotate(angleDeg: number, cx = 0, cy = 0): number[] {
  const a = Math.cos((angleDeg * Math.PI) / 180);
  const b = Math.sin((angleDeg * Math.PI) / 180);
  // rotate around (cx, cy)
  return multiplyMatrices(
    translate(cx, cy),
    multiplyMatrices([a, b, -b, a, 0, 0], translate(-cx, -cy)),
  );
}

export function scale(sx: number, sy = sx): number[] {
  return [sx, 0, 0, sy, 0, 0];
}
```

---

### 4. Path & Shape Primitives

```ts
// src/core/primitives.ts
import { idGen, identityMatrix } from "./utils";
import { BaseObject, Attributes, Transform, Point, Color } from "./types";

export class Path implements BaseObject {
  id: string;
  type = "path";
  attrs: Attributes = {};

  constructor(public d: string, attrs?: Partial<Attributes>) {
    this.id = idGen();
    if (attrs) Object.assign(this.attrs, attrs);
  }

  transform(matrix: number[]): void {
    this.transform.matrix = multiplyMatrices(this.transform.matrix, matrix);
  }

  get transform(): Transform {
    return this._transform || identityMatrix();
  }

  set transform(value: Transform) {
    this._transform = value;
  }

  private _transform?: Transform;
}
```

You can extend the `Path` class to support `addCurve`, `addLine`, `addEllipse`, `addRect`, etc., by exposing builder methods.

---

### 5. Group & Layer

```ts
// src/core/group.ts
import { BaseObject, Layer } from "./types";
import { idGen, identityMatrix } from "./utils";

export class Group implements BaseObject {
  id: string;
  type = "group";
  attrs: {} = {};
  children: BaseObject[] = [];
  transform: Transform = identityMatrix();

  constructor(public name = "Group") {
    this.id = idGen();
  }

  add(obj: BaseObject) {
    this.children.push(obj);
  }

  remove(obj: BaseObject) {
    this.children = this.children.filter(o => o !== obj);
  }
}
```

---

### 6. Document & Layer Management

```ts
// src/core/document.ts
import { Layer } from "./types";
import { idGen } from "./utils";

export class Document {
  layers: Layer[] = [];
  width: number; height: number;

  constructor(width: number, height: number) {
    this.width = width;
    this.height = height;
    this.createLayer("Background");
  }

  createLayer(name = "Layer"): Layer {
    const layer: Layer = { name, objects: [] };
    this.layers.push(layer);
    return layer;
  }

  deleteLayer(layer: Layer) {
    this.layers = this.layers.filter(l => l !== layer);
  }

  findLayer(name: string): Layer | undefined {
    return this.layers.find(l => l.name === name);
  }
}
```

---

### 7. SVG Import/Export

```ts
// src/io/svg.ts
import { Document, Path, Group, Layer } from "../core";
import { DOMParser } from "xmldom";
import * as xpath from "xpath";

/* NOTE: In a real project you probably want to use a proper SVG parser
   library (svgo, svgson, etc.). This is illustrative only. */

export function exportSvg(doc: Document): string {
  // Basic header
  const header = `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="${doc.width}" height="${doc.height}">`;

  const body = doc.layers
    .map(layer => {
      const groupId = `layer-${layer.name.replace(/\s+/g, "_")}`;
      return `<g id="${groupId}" data-layer-name="${layer.name}">${layer.objects
        .map(obj => objectToSvg(obj))
        .join("")}</g>`;
    })
    .join("");
  return `${header}${body}</svg>`;
}

function objectToSvg(obj: any): string {
  if (obj.type === "path") {
    const { d, attrs, transform } = obj;
    const style = attrsToStyle(attrs);
    const matrix = transformAsAttribute(transform);
    return `<path d="${d}" style="${style}" transform="${matrix}" />`;
  }
  // add group handling etc.
  return "";
}

function attrsToStyle(attrs: any): string {
  const parts: string[] = [];
  if (attrs.fill) parts.push(`fill:${attrs.fill}`);
  if (attrs.stroke) parts.push(`stroke:${attrs.stroke}`);
  if (attrs.strokeWidth) parts.push(`stroke-width:${attrs.strokeWidth}`);
  if (attrs.opacity) parts.push(`opacity:${attrs.opacity}`);
  return parts.join(";");
}

function transformAsAttribute({ matrix }: { matrix: number[] }) {
  const [a, b, c, d, e, f] = matrix;
  return `matrix(${a},${b},${c},${d},${e},${f})`;
}

export function importSvg(svgText: string): Document {
  const dom = new DOMParser().parseFromString(svgText, "image/svg+xml");
  const width = parseInt(dom.documentElement.getAttribute("width") || "0");
  const height = parseInt(dom.documentElement.getAttribute("height") || "0");
  const doc = new Document(width, height);

  const layerNodes = xpath.select(
    "//*[local-name()='g' and @data-layer-name]",
    dom,
  ) as any[];

  for (const layerNode of layerNodes) {
    const name = layerNode.getAttribute("data-layer-name") || "Unnamed";
    const layer = doc.createLayer(name);
    const pathNodes = xpath.select("./* [local-name()='path']", layerNode) as any[];

    for (const p of pathNodes) {
      const d = p.getAttribute("d") || "";
      const style = p.getAttribute("style") || "";
      const attrs = parseStyle(style);
      const transform = transformFromAttribute(p.getAttribute("transform") || "");
      layer.objects.push(new Path(d, attrs));
      // note: apply transform later if desired
    }
  }

  return doc;
}

function parseStyle(styleText: string) {
  const attrs: any = {};
  for (const part of styleText.split(";")) {
    const [k, v] = part.split(":");
    if (k && v) attrs[k.trim()] = v.trim();
  }
  return attrs;
}

function transformFromAttribute(attr: string) {
  /* Very naive parser – only supports `matrix(...)` */
  const m = attr.match(/matrix\(([^)]*)\)/);
  if (!m) return identityMatrix();
  const nums = m[1].split(",").map(parseFloat);
  return { matrix: nums };
}
```

---

### 8. Public API

```ts
// src/index.ts
export { Document, Layer, Path, Group } from "./core";
export { exportSvg, importSvg } from "./io/svg";
```

---

## How to Use it

```ts
import { Document, Path, exportSvg } from "mini-illustrator";

/* 1. Create a doc */
const doc = new Document(800, 600);

/* 2. Add a simple rectangle (implemented as a path) */
const rect = new Path(
  "M0 0 L200 0 L200 100 L0 100 Z",
  { fill: "#ff0000", stroke: "#000000", strokeWidth: 2 },
);
doc.layers[0].objects.push(rect);

/* 3. Export to SVG */
const svgText = exportSvg(doc);
console.log(svgText);
```

---

## Extending It

| Feature | Where to add it | Quick notes |
|---------|-----------------|-------------|
| **Text** | `src/core/primitives.ts` – add a `Text` class | Use SVG `<text>` element |
| **Gradients** | Create a `Gradient` class, serialize as `<defs>` block | Store in `Document.defs` |
| **Clipping & Masks** | Add `clipPath`/`mask` utilities | Store as separate objects |
| **Brushes / Patterns** | Use SVG patterns `<pattern>` | Handle data URIs or external images |
| **Undo/Redo** | Add `History` buffer in `Document` | Store serialized states |
| **GUI** | Build an Electron or web front‑end | Connect `Document` to canvas or SVG view |

---

## Why Not Write “Full Illustrator”?

* The **AI file format** is proprietary; reverse‑engineering it would involve a lot of legal and technical risk.
* Illustrator supports **hundreds of layers, 3‑d transforms, advanced pixel manipulation, real‑time effects, GPU acceleration**, etc. These are outside the scope of a simple library.
* For interoperable vector graphics, **SVG** is the de‑facto standard. It’s readable, editable, and works in Illustrator without any conversion.

---

## Wrap‑Up

The code above gives you a **solid backbone** for a vector graphics engine that feels “Illustrator‑like” in spirit:

- **Modular** – add shapes, transforms, or layers as you wish.
- **Type‑safe** – easy to reason about objects.
- **Exportable** – you can open the resulting SVG in Adobe Illustrator or any other vector editor.

You can now fork it into your own project, add UI, or expand the engine. Happy coding!

